    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nO Donnellan & Joyce are delighted to offer for sale this lovely five bed detached home located in the popular and scenic townland of Killola, Rosscahill, Co. Galway.\n\nLocated approximately 5km from the village of Oughterard, and just 9km from Moycullen, with both villages offering an abundance of shops, lively pubs, bank, hotels, post office and restaurants.\n\nIn terms of schools, Oughterard & Moycullen offer several primary and secondary school options that serve the local community and surrounding Connemara areas\n\nOughterard Golf Course is just 3km and there is also a host of GAA, equestrian, sailing, cycling, and athletics clubs within the surrounding area.\n\nKillola, Rosscahill is set back off the road on a large site offering complete privacy. Externally the site offers ample off-street parking and gardens to the front, side and rear.\n\nThe property is located adjacent to the proposed new greenway which will provide a superb natural recreational amenity on completion. \n\nAccommodation consists of a bright and spacious entrance hall, a lounge room with feature wood flooring and insert stove, a large open plan kitchen and dining room with feature solid fuel stove with stone surround. \n\nAlso on the ground floor is the main bathroom and three large bedrooms two of which offer en suite bathrooms. A utility and laundry room to the rear completes the ground floor.\n\nOn the first floor the property offers a storage room and two large bedrooms, both with plumbing available for en-suite bathrooms.\n \nThe beautiful Lough Corrib is close by, public slips and extensive moorings available in the village of Oughterard, making it the ideal location for any fishing & boating enthusiast. \n\nKnown as the Gateway to Connemara via Maam Cross with large numbers of visitors flocking to the area each year. It is renowned for its natural beauty with walking routes, boating facilities and other outdoor leisure activities, offering all that one could require in terms of modern day living. \n\nHomes in this idyllic location rarely come to the market, making this an ideal property for any buyer looking for a tranquil rural lifestyle but still near all essential amenities. \n\nViewing recommended & guaranteed not to disappoint.Properties can be viewed on our website www.odj.ie Keep up to-date with NEW PROPERTIES by registering your details on our database For Further details please contact O'Donnellan & Joyce on 091-564212 OFFICE OPENING HOURS - MON TO FRI 9AM TO 5:30PMNOTE: These particulars are not to be considered a formal offer. They are for information only and give a general idea of the property. They are not to be taken as forming any part of a resulting contract, nor to be relied upon as statements or representations of fact.FLOORPLANS: The floor plan including furniture, fixture measurements and dimensions are approximate and for illustrative purposes only. The Polycam App used gives no guarantee, warranty or representation as to the accuracy and layout. All enquiries must be directed to the agent.Whilst every care is taken in their preparation, neither O'Donnellan & Joyce Auctioneers nor the vendor accept any liability as to their accuracy. Intending purchasers must satisfy themselves by personal inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of these particulars.No person in the employment of O'Donnellan & Joyce Auctioneers has any authority to make or give any representation or warranty whatever in relation to this property."
      },
      {
